From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shi Jiayang <shi05275@163.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: pass bridge multicast snooping changes to drivers

A bridge announces a change of its multicast snooping state with
SWITCHDEV_ATTR_ID_BRIDGE_MC_DISABLED, but DSA has no handler for it. A
switch that holds permanent MDB entries in hardware keeps forwarding by
them while the bridge floods multicast.

Add an optional port_bridge_mcast_snooping operation and call it for that
attribute, so a driver can remove or replay its MDB entries. Drivers that
do not implement it behave as before.

Signed-off-by: Shi Jiayang <shi05275@163.com>
---
--- a/include/net/dsa.h
+++ b/include/net/dsa.h
@@ -1055,6 +1055,9 @@ struct dsa_switch_ops {
 				     struct netlink_ext_ack *extack);
 	void	(*port_set_host_flood)(struct dsa_switch *ds, int port,
 				       bool uc, bool mc);
+	/* Synchronize static multicast entries with bridge snooping changes. */
+	int	(*port_bridge_mcast_snooping)(struct dsa_switch *ds, int port,
+					      bool enabled);
 
 	/*
 	 * VLAN support
--- a/net/dsa/user.c
+++ b/net/dsa/user.c
@@ -620,6 +620,15 @@ static int dsa_user_port_attr_set(struct
 
 		ret = dsa_port_vlan_protocol(dp, attr->u.vlan_protocol, extack);
 		break;
+	case SWITCHDEV_ATTR_ID_BRIDGE_MC_DISABLED:
+		if ((!dsa_port_offloads_bridge_dev(dp, attr->orig_dev) &&
+		     !dsa_port_offloads_bridge_port(dp, attr->orig_dev)) ||
+		    !dp->ds->ops->port_bridge_mcast_snooping)
+			return -EOPNOTSUPP;
+
+		ret = dp->ds->ops->port_bridge_mcast_snooping(dp->ds, dp->index,
+							    !attr->u.mc_disabled);
+		break;
 	case SWITCHDEV_ATTR_ID_BRIDGE_AGEING_TIME:
 		if (!dsa_port_offloads_bridge_dev(dp, attr->orig_dev))
 			return -EOPNOTSUPP;
